WEBVTT

00:00:02.333 --> 00:00:07.966
Let's take an idea through Thoock, from researching an opportunity to preparing an export package.

00:00:07.966 --> 00:00:11.346
Start by giving the next batch a clear direction.

00:00:12.875 --> 00:00:15.368
For a new batch, start in Opportunities.

00:00:15.368 --> 00:00:18.931
Add a topic, import your research, or use AI research.

00:00:18.931 --> 00:00:24.631
Choose an idea based on the buyer, market, and type of image you want to create.

00:00:26.166 --> 00:00:31.397
Open Commercial briefs to give each image a buyer, a purpose, and a visual direction.

00:00:31.397 --> 00:00:38.022
You can add a brief manually, or choose Create with AI to build a batch from a saved opportunity.

00:00:38.022 --> 00:00:40.812
Review the brief before using it in generation.

00:00:42.333 --> 00:00:48.483
In Image generation, select your brief and choose a provider, model, aspect ratio, and resolution.

00:00:48.483 --> 00:00:53.813
Check the prompt, then review the generation request and confirm when you're ready.

00:00:53.813 --> 00:00:57.913
AI features use your own provider key and billing account.

00:00:59.416 --> 00:01:01.692
Open History to follow the generation.

00:01:01.692 --> 00:01:05.864
Once it finishes, head to Review queue to inspect the results.

00:01:05.864 --> 00:01:12.312
If a request fails, open its provider log to see what happened before deciding whether to retry.

00:01:13.833 --> 00:01:18.931
In Review queue, inspect your images and choose the ones you want to keep.

00:01:18.931 --> 00:01:24.393
If you already have images, use Import images to bring them into the same workflow.

00:01:24.393 --> 00:01:29.127
Check composition and technical quality, look for defects, and complete the review checks.

00:01:30.666 --> 00:01:36.865
Select the images you want to describe, then choose Generate AI metadata to create a draft.

00:01:36.865 --> 00:01:40.351
Check each title, keyword list, and category before approval.

00:01:40.351 --> 00:01:45.000
Make sure the details describe what is actually visible in the image.

00:01:46.541 --> 00:01:50.176
In Adobe exports, select the approved images for your batch.

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:52.720
Click Prepare package and enter a name.

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:55.991
Confirm the package, then choose where to save it.

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:00.560
Open Export batches to find your saved package.

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:05.914
Check the prepared images and Adobe CSV before uploading them through your stock platform.

00:02:05.914 --> 00:02:11.269
You can return to this history whenever you need to find a package again.

00:02:12.791 --> 00:02:16.713
Return to the dashboard to see what needs your attention next.

00:02:16.713 --> 00:02:20.634
Continue a brief, review more candidates, or prepare the next export.

00:02:20.634 --> 00:02:24.555
Use the same workflow whenever you are ready for another batch.
